 "narrative": "The newly released independent validations complete and strengthen the core dataset associations. For H5 SMARCA4 loss, the discovery signed mean difference was +0.833 composite units, and independent validation gave +0.795 with interval +0.695 to +0.896 under the stricter validation alpha. The estimate is far above the 0.15-unit threshold in the negative raw exposed-minus-comparator direction, so SMARCA4 loss is associated with a lower composite dependency score, i.e., stronger measured dependency. I accept H5 and close the main-effect investigation because validation supports the discovery result. For H3 TP53 loss, independent validation gave a signed mean difference of +0.471 with interval +0.334 to +0.607, alongside discovery +0.423 with interval +0.327 to +0.520. Both are above the threshold in the claimed positive raw direction, corresponding to a higher composite score and therefore weaker measured dependency. I accept H3 and close the main-effect investigation. For H24, the conditional comparison of SMARCA4 loss within KEAP1-loss-positive lines received independent validation: signed mean difference +0.926 with interval +0.741 to +1.110, beyond discovery +0.809 with interval +0.678 to +0.940. This remains a large effect in the negative raw direction, showing that SMARCA4-loss association is not eliminated when KEAP1 loss is present. I accept H24 and close that conditional claim. Together with already validated KEAP1 loss H7 and accepted conditional claims, the supplied dataset now supports three highly separable, robust predictor-composite associations: SMARCA4 loss associated with stronger measured dependency; KEAP1 loss and TP53 loss associated with weaker measured dependency. The evidence does not establish causal gene-level dependence because the endpoint is a composite score and associations may reflect correlated genomic or processing states. Negative findings remain important: lineage subtype, KRAS, MTAP, PIK3CA, MYC amplification, constructed research markers, STK11, ARID1A, RB1, BRCA2 loss, and Avana-library main effect did not support their registered threshold-level claims. Original PTEN positive-direction claim was rejected because the observed contrast was opposite; the reversed PTEN claim is currently only borderline because its signed estimate is above threshold but the lower confidence bound is below the 0.15-unit threshold. The most informative next analyses are the registered PTEN reverse main/conditional comparisons H50-H51, the CDKN2A double-negative conditional claim H52, remaining broad screens H40-H43, remaining technical audits H33-H35, and the context interactions H44-H49.",
 "research_notes": "Current accepted core dataset associations: H5 SMARCA4 loss -> lower composite / stronger measured dependency, validated and main closed; H3 TP53 loss -> higher composite / weaker measured dependency, validated and main closed; H7 KEAP1 loss -> higher composite / weaker measured dependency, validated and main closed. Conditional/robustness claims accepted: H24 SMARCA4 within KEAP1-loss-positive, now validated and closed; H13-H17, H29-H32, H36-H38 confirm conditional separability of TP53/SMARCA4/KEAP1 associations. Interaction structure: SMARCA4-by-KEAP1 interactions H25-H26 rejected; TP53-by-SMARCA4 H27 rejected; TP53-by-KEAP1 H28 unresolved borderline positive interaction +0.210 with lower bound below threshold. Additional screens: H19 CDKN2A unresolved borderline +0.141 [0.062,0.220]; H50 PTEN reversed main is unresolved, signed +0.227 but lower bound +0.131 below threshold and no independent validation; H51/H52 registered PTEN and CDKN2A double-negative conditional follow-ups. Negative/no-threshold findings: H1 lineage subtype, H2 KRAS, H4 MTAP, H6 PIK3CA, H8 MYC amplification, H9-H11 research markers D/E/F, H12 KRAS by marker D, H18 STK11, H20 ARID1A, H22 RB1, H23 Avana-library main effect, H39 BRCA2 loss. Unresolved/pending: H28 TP53-by-KEAP1 interaction, H33-H35 technical audits, H40 NF1, H41 MSI-high, H42 sex, H43 media serum, H44-H49 histology/library interactions, H50-H52 PTEN/CDKN2A follow-ups. Most informative next analysis: evaluate H50-H52 first; if PTEN reverse association remains coherent and exceeds threshold in conditional/uncertainty sense, consider independent validation. Then run context interactions and technical audits. Interpret all accepted results as associations within the supplied composite dependency dataset, not causal single-gene claims or externally generalizable claims."
}

