  "narrative": "The new discovery results mainly resolve context probes and technical audits rather than adding many new core effects. Direct KEAP1-loss effects are large in both lineage subtypes: squamous +0.877 and adenocarcinoma +0.814 signed units, both far above the 0.15 threshold with intervals well above zero. This supports H86/H87 and lets me close the lineage-subtype KEAP1 interaction H45 as unsupported. Direct TP53-loss effects are also meaningful in both lineage subtypes: squamous +0.447 and adenocarcinoma +0.414, supporting H88/H89 and closing H46. For SMARCA4, the direct lineage strata are both strong, and the interaction estimate H44 does not have a lower bound above the meaningful threshold, so H44 is rejected as a lineage modification.\n\nFor the constructed research_signature_b context, H85 shows a strong positive TP53-loss association in the low-signature-b complement: +0.556, lower bound +0.459, consistent with the usual weaker-dependency TP53 association. H84, the high-signature-b direct stratum, has point estimate +0.224 signed to the negative raw direction but interval lower -0.047, so the direct within-stratum estimate is underpowered and cannot be accepted. I leave H84 unresolved but closed because the validated H82 interaction already provides the stronger inference that the TP53-loss association is attenuated or reversed relative to the complement in high-signature-b lines. By contrast, the analogous signature-b interactions for KEAP1 and SMARCA4 are only borderline, with intervals crossing zero and lower bounds below the threshold; I reject H73 and H74. The signature-c negative-control interaction H91 is near null, which argues against broad constructed-signature context dependence and supports assay-specific or chance-specific findings. H73/H74/H91 should therefore be treated as dataset-context probes, not causal or generalizable biology.\n\nH92 gives the most refined CDKN2A-loss estimate: +0.164 in TP53-, KEAP1-, SMARCA4-, and PTEN-intact lines, but its lower bound +0.101 is below the 0.15 meaningful threshold. Combined with prior CDKN2A estimates around 0.12-0.14, this does not support a scientifically meaningful CDKN2A-loss effect, so I reject the CDKN2A claims rather than continue to allocate resources to a consistently near-threshold signal. The technical matched RNA/DNA audit H35 is also near null and is rejected/closed, providing reassurance against a broad sample-data-availability confound.\n\nThe most important new direct finding is H90: MSI-high lines show a very strong stronger-dependency association after restricting to TP53-intact, SMARCA4-intact, and KEAP1-intact lines, signed +0.745 with lower bound +0.666. This is large and statistically compelling in the supplied data, but the exposed MSI-high cell is only n=62. Because the effect is both novel and important, I accept H90 provisionally in this dataset and request independent validation. I choose H90 over H65 for validation because H90 is a new direct conditional predictor with a small exposed cell, whereas H65 is a constructed-assay interaction that remains accepted discovery-only and can be validated later if needed. None of these claims should be interpreted as causal or generalizable beyond this supplied dataset.",
  "research_notes": "Current core accepted associations in this dataset: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger dependency; KEAP1 loss -> weaker dependency; TP53 loss -> weaker dependency; PTEN loss -> stronger dependency mainly in TP53-intact/other-intact contexts; MSI-high -> stronger dependency overall and after removing TP53/SMARCA4/KEAP1 contexts (H90 accepted, validation pending). Lineage subtype does not appear to materially modify SMARCA4, KEAP1, or TP53 core associations: H44/H45/H46 rejected after direct stratum tests. Constructed research_signature_b strongly modifies TP53-loss association (H82 validated); signature_b does not support KEAP1 or SMARCA4 modification (H73/H74 rejected); signature_c is null (H91). H65 signature_a interaction remains accepted discovery-only and is not independently validated; keep as a lower-priority validation candidate. CDKN2A-loss effects are repeatedly below or not threshold-supported once uncertainty and context restrictions are considered; H19/H52/H57/H71/H92 closed as rejected. Technical audits: matched RNA/DNA availability near null (H35), batch A vs B near null (H81), Avana library main and interaction effects not meaningful, KY library not supporting claimed positive effect. H84 direct high-signature_b TP53 stratum is underpowered and unresolved but closed. Next priority: assess H90 independent validation. If H90 validates, MSI-high becomes one of the strongest supported associations. If H90 fails validation, downgrade conditional MSI-high while retaining broader H41 only if still reasonable. Avoid causal and generalizability language for constructed assays and thresholded interactions."
}

