  "narrative": "The due validation results resolve several context questions, but they do not add another broadly robust new association beyond the already accepted core set. H72 claimed a positive TP53-loss interaction in the high research_signature_b stratum, but both discovery and independent validation are negative when signed to that claimed +1 direction: discovery -0.780 and validation -0.570. The opposite-direction claim H82, however, is accepted and independently validated. Thus the evidence supports an attenuated or reversed relative TP53-loss association in high research_signature_b lines, but not the originally oriented H72 claim; H72 is rejected and closed. H25 and H26 test the reciprocal SMARCA4-loss-by-KEAP1-loss interaction. Discovery and validation are both near null: H25 validation is +0.149 with strict interval -0.079 to +0.376, and H26 validation is +0.021 with strict interval -0.174 to +0.217. Neither interval provides robust evidence for a meaningful interaction beyond the 0.15-unit threshold. I therefore keep both interaction claims rejected and close them. The most important reassessment is H93, MSI-high status within TP53-loss lines. The discovery estimate was large, +0.884 signed units with lower bound +0.455, but only 24 exposed observations. Independent validation was directionally consistent, +0.628, but its strict lower bound was only +0.032 and the exposed validation cell was only 29 observations. The validation does not contradict the direction, but it also does not independently establish a meaningful effect at the threshold. Because this rare-cell conditional claim was accepted mainly to test whether MSI-high remains meaningful in a TP53-loss background, and independent validation did not clear the threshold, I downgrade H93 to unresolved and close further investigation. This does not undermine the broader MSI-high result: MSI-high remains a strong supplied-dataset association overall and in multiple other contexts.\n\nOverall supported dataset-internal associations. SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger measured dependency: the main effect H5 is large and independently validated, and the effect remains strong in TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact, TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, and both lineage strata. KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker measured dependency: main effect H7 is large and validated, and the direct effect remains large within TP53-intact, SMARCA4-intact, TP53-loss, and both lineage strata; within TP53-loss lines H100 is +0.990 signed with lower bound +0.809. TP53 loss is associated with weaker measured dependency overall H3, validated, and in TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact and lineage strata. PTEN loss is not supported as a simple overall main effect, but it is associated with stronger measured dependency in TP53-intact contexts: H58 is independently validated and closed, H67 is independently validated and closed, and H99 is accepted as a direct KEAP1-loss stratum estimate. MSI-high is one of the strongest supplied-dataset associations: H41 overall is accepted; H90 triple-intact context is independently validated; H83, H94, and H95 remain strong in other direct contexts. The H93 TP53-loss context is now unresolved because of validation uncertainty, not because its point estimate reverses. The constructed assay result for high research_signature_b and TP53 loss H82 is independently validated as a reversed/attenuated relative interaction, but because the assay is constructed and the threshold is analysis-defined, it should remain a dataset-internal statistical observation rather than biological mechanism. The lower-threshold research_signature_a interaction H104, and the earlier high-threshold H65, remain discovery-supported but constructed-assay-dependent.\n\nNegative findings are broad. There is no meaningful lineage-subtype main effect or lineage-subtype modification of SMARCA4, KEAP1, or TP53 associations. There is no meaningful SMARCA4-by-KEAP1 interaction. There is no meaningful main effect of APC mutation, APC-by-Wnt interaction, PTEN-by-PIK3CA interaction, SMARCA4-by-stemness interaction, TP53-by-high-mutation-burden interaction, KRAS, MTAP, MYC amplification, ARID1A, BRCA2, NF1, RB1, SMAD4, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, STK11, PIK3CA, or CDKN2A after multiple contextual probes. The constructed binary research markers are null. Technical and assay-availability probes are mostly null, including matched RNA/DNA availability, batch A versus batch B, Avana library main effect, media-serum contrast, and sex; some technical claims remain untested but are low priority. The research_marker and signature probes indicate that not every constructed assay carries dependency signal.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty is concentrated in rare cells, constructed assays, and untested context probes. The most important unresolved scientific uncertainty is H93: the TP53-loss conditional MSI-high effect remains uncertain because of small exposed cells. The second is the constructed research_signature_a interaction family H65/H104, which remains accepted discovery-only and has not been independently validated or mechanistically contextualized. The registered direct strata H105 and H106 are the most informative next analyses because they ask whether the interaction is driven by a meaningful direct TP53-loss effect in research_signature_a >=0 lines versus the complement. H107 may also clarify the PTEN-loss context, but H105/H106 are more valuable because they directly test the currently fragile constructed-signature claim. If continuing, I would prioritize H105 and H106; if they are not supported or do not explain H65/H104, I would close the signature_a TP53 interaction as an analysis-dependent or chance-driven feature of this supplied dataset. All conclusions remain associations within the supplied data, not causal effects, and generalizability beyond this dataset remains unestablished.",
  "research_notes": "Final-stage synthesis at iteration 8. Due validations: H72 rejected because signed evidence is opposite its +1 direction; reversed H82 accepted/validated. H25/H26 rejected/closed: no SMARCA4-by-KEAP1 interaction. H93 downgraded to unresolved/closed: MSI-high in TP53-loss has positive discovery +0.884 (n=24) and positive validation +0.628 but validation strict lower +0.032 below 0.15 threshold; not robust enough to retain as supported. Broad MSI-high supported by H41 overall accepted, H90 triple-intact accepted/validated, H83 TP53/SMARCA4-intact accepted, H94 KEAP1-loss accepted, H95 SMARCA4-loss accepted.\n\nSupported dataset-internal core effects: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger dependency, accepted/validated; KEAP1 loss -> weaker dependency, accepted/validated and strong across TP53/SMARCA4/lineage contexts incl H100; TP53 loss -> weaker dependency, accepted/validated main and lineage/core-intact contexts; PTEN loss -> stronger dependency conditional, especially TP53-intact H58/H67 validated and H99 in KEAP1-loss accepted; MSI-high -> stronger dependency broadly. Constructed assay: H82 high research_signature_b attenuates/reverses TP53 interaction, accepted/validated but not biological. H65/H104 research_signature_a TP53 interactions accepted discovery-only, constructed/threshold-dependent, active.\n\nMajor negatives: lineage main/interactions, markers, APC, Wnt interaction, PTEN-by-PIK3CA, SMARCA4-by-stemness, TP53-by-mutation_burden, many mutation main effects, CDKN2A cluster, technical batch/omics/media/sex. Unresolved: H93 TP53-loss MSI context; H65/H104 constructed interaction family; H105/H106 direct sig_a TP53 strata; H107 optional; H101 hypoxia/KEAP1 untested; some technical claims. Next priority: run H105/H106 to determine whether H65/H104 reflect meaningful direct strata or threshold/constructed artifact. Do not infer causality or external generalizability."
