  "narrative": "No independent validation can be requested because the remaining voluntary validation budget is zero; the validate field is therefore omitted. I assessed each newly delivered discovery comparison against the 0.15 composite-dependency-unit threshold and the 95% Welch interval, treating the supplied estimates as already signed to the registered direction.\n\nThe accepted results are H139, H140, H142, and H143. H139 shows that in KEAP1-loss, TP53-intact, SMARCA4-intact lines, PTEN loss remains associated with stronger dependency with signed estimate +0.390 and lower bound +0.202. This is important because it indicates that the previously accepted KEAP1-loss/TP53-intact PTEN association (H107) is not merely carried by overlap with SMARCA4-loss lines. The exposed cell is modest (n=36), so I treat this as a dataset-internal conditional confirmation rather than a new core predictor.\n\nH140 is a large interaction: in the core-intact TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact background, the PTEN-loss stronger-dependency association is substantially larger in research_signature_a >= 0 than in its complement, signed estimate +0.596 and lower bound +0.464. This is internally coherent with the direct high-research_signature_a PTEN effect H117 (+0.576, lower +0.462, independently validated) and the low-research_signature_a direct test H127 (null/opposite). I accept H140 as a dataset-internal specificity boundary, not as evidence for biology or generalizability.\n\nH142 and H143 strongly support technical robustness of two core effects under higher Cas9 activity. In high-Cas9, TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact lines, SMARCA4 loss remains associated with stronger dependency, signed estimate +0.796, lower +0.720. In high-Cas9, TP53-intact, SMARCA4-intact lines, KEAP1 loss remains associated with weaker dependency, signed estimate +0.754, lower +0.680. These effects are very large and well above threshold, so the broad SMARCA4 and KEAP1 findings are not explained away by Cas9-activity confounding at this restricted high-activity stratum.\n\nH146 does not meet the threshold-clearing standard. In high-Cas9, TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact lines, PTEN loss has signed estimate +0.204 but lower bound +0.092, below the 0.15-unit threshold. It is directionally positive and consistent with smaller PTEN effects, but it cannot be accepted as scientifically meaningful. I reject the direct threshold claim and close it, while noting that it should reduce confidence in a uniform PTEN effect across Cas9-activity contexts rather than overturn the broader validated TP53-intact and KEAP1-loss conditional PTEN findings.\n\nH141 is also not threshold-clearing: PTEN loss in core-intact positive research_signature_b lines has signed estimate +0.098 and lower bound +0.001. It is directionally positive and statistically near-zero, but the point estimate is below the scientific threshold and the interval includes values below it. I reject the claim of a scientifically meaningful direct PTEN effect in high research_signature_b. This prevents overextending the constructed research_signature_a specificity to all positive constructed signatures.\n\nH127 rejects PTEN loss in core-intact low research_signature_a lines: signed estimate -0.020 with interval -0.089 to +0.049. This directly supports interpretation of the high-research_signature_a PTEN finding as a specificity boundary or attenuation contrast, not a uniform low-signature PTEN effect.\n\nThe interaction panel is largely negative. H128 PTEN-by-MYC-high interaction is small and crosses zero, +0.084, -0.108 to +0.277. H130 PTEN-by-ploidy-high interaction is -0.046, -0.238 to +0.146. H131 PTEN-by-growth-rate-high interaction is +0.035, -0.177 to +0.247. H132 PTEN-by-EMT-high interaction is -0.019, -0.212 to +0.173. H134 SMARCA4-by-MYC-high interaction is -0.107, -0.240 to +0.026. None clears the threshold; all are opposite or near-null. This argues against MYC expression, ploidy, growth rate, or EMT as important modifiers of PTEN context specificity in this dataset, and against additional MYC-high modification of SMARCA4 loss beyond the already very broad SMARCA4 association.\n\nThe main audit concerns remain multiplicity, constructed-assay dependence, and small exposed cells in several conditional strata. The large lower bounds for H139, H140, H142, and H143 make chance alone less plausible for those specific comparisons, but they do not establish causality, biological interpretation, or external generalization. They remain supplied-dataset associations. The interaction negatives are useful because they prevent overinterpretation of the PTEN conditional effects as generic proliferation or stress-state effects.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 11 appraise update: No validation remains. Accepted/closed: H139, H140, H142, H143. Rejected/closed: H127, H141, H146, H128, H130, H131, H132, H134.\n\nInterpretation: PTEN conditional stronger-dependency effects survive removal of SMARCA4-loss lines within KEAP1-loss/TP53-intact context (H139), and the high-research_signature_a direct effect H117 is now supported by an accepted core-intact interaction H140 plus null low-signature H127. This strengthens the PTEN high-signature specificity boundary, but the PTEN claim remains dataset-internal and should not be generalized as biology. High-Cas9 strata preserve the core SMARCA4-loss stronger-dependency and KEAP1-loss weaker-dependency associations very strongly, reducing concern that these two headline associations are Cas9-activity artifacts. High-Cas9 PTEN direct test H146 is not threshold-clearing, so PTEN effects are less uniformly robust than SMARCA4/KEAP1 effects and may be sensitive to editing-activity context or smaller sample size.\n\nThe research_signature_b direct PTEN test H141 is small/borderline and rejected for practical importance. The null MYC/ploidy/growth/EMT interactions against PTEN, and null SMARCA4-by-MYC interaction, argue against additional molecular modifiers for those core associations within the tested median/threshold strata. The core dataset-internal model remains: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger dependency; KEAP1 loss -> weaker dependency; TP53 loss -> weaker dependency overall but attenuated in high constructed research_signature_a/b; MSI-high -> strong stronger dependency broadly; PTEN loss -> conditional stronger dependency primarily in TP53-intact, selected KEAP1/signature backgrounds, not uniform. No causal or external claims."
