  "research_notes": "Iteration 13 appraise update. Voluntary validation is exhausted; future work can only refine supplied-dataset internal inference. The PTEN-loss audit is now strongly bounded: PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency in TP53-intact elevated research_signature_a contexts, accepted in high-Cas9 and low-Cas9 strata and in high-screen_roc_auc stratum, with no accepted Cas9 or screen_roc_auc modifier, and with signature specificity retained within high-quality TP53-intact lines. Low-signature PTEN tests remain near-null. Thus PTEN loss is not a global predictor; it is a narrow TP53-intact/high-research_signature_a associated predictor, with evidence of internal technical robustness but not external validation or mechanism. The broader model remains SMARCA4-loss stronger dependency, KEAP1-loss weaker dependency, MSI-high stronger dependency, TP53-loss overall weaker dependency attenuated in high constructed signature strata, and PTEN-loss context-specific stronger dependency. Screen-quality interactions for core predictors and an older-age SMARCA4 interaction were not supported at threshold and are closed; remaining analogous age probes are deferred. New proposals extend PTEN robustness using screen_nnmd, test direct core effects in high-screen-quality and older-age strata, and test batch_a interactions for core predictors."
