  "narrative": "With the independent validation budget exhausted and no assessments due, this explore stage focuses the remaining discovery effort on the least-settled part of the evidence base: whether PTEN-loss associations are robust technical or biological context effects rather than artifacts of sparse strata, screen quality, Cas9 quality, chromosomal-instability proxies, or constructed-signature positivity. The core associations for SMARCA4 loss (stronger dependency), KEAP1 loss (weaker dependency), MSI-high (stronger dependency), and TP53 loss (weaker dependency) are already accepted in many strata and some have independent validation, so repeating them is lower value. By contrast, PTEN loss has repeatedly accepted evidence in TP53-intact, research_signature_a-positive backgrounds, but several broader lineage and instability contexts remain unresolved. I registered four refinements: PTEN loss in the accepted triple-intact TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact, research_signature_a-positive context with high screen ROC quality; PTEN loss in the same triple-intact context with above-median Cas9 activity; PTEN loss among TP53-intact squamous lines that are research_signature_a-positive, complementing the accepted adenocarcinoma context; and PTEN loss among TP53-intact research_signature_a-positive lines with high aneuploidy, testing whether unresolved TP53-intact high-aneuploidy PTEN evidence becomes clear once the accepted signature context is added. These are falsifiable dataset-internal comparisons, not causal effects, single-gene knockout claims, or external generalizations. Direction convention: direction -1 claims a more negative exposed-minus-comparator composite score, i.e., stronger dependency. Results will be interpreted only if every comparison cell has at least 20 observations and signed 95% Welch lower bounds exceed the 0.15 composite-dependency-unit threshold.",
  "research_notes": "ITER19 EXPLORE: validation budget exhausted; no new validation possible. Current dataset-internal accepted core findings: SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency (direction -1), KEAP1 loss weaker dependency (direction +1), MSI-high stronger dependency (direction -1), TP53 loss weaker dependency (direction +1). PTEN loss is context-sensitive: strongest accepted evidence is in TP53-intact and research_signature_a-positive contexts, including triple-intact TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact contexts and some screen/Cas9/growth halves; global or unconditioned PTEN effects are not uniform and some lineage or aneuploidy strata remain borderline. Active unresolved probes already registered: H250/H251 (PTEN triple-intact sig_a+ split by high/low aneuploidy) and H252/H253 (TP53 loss by Cas9 activity high/low). New registered refinements test: (1) PTEN triple-intact sig_a+ high screen ROC; (2) PTEN triple-intact sig_a+ high Cas9; (3) PTEN TP53-intact sig_a+ squamous, complementing accepted adenocarcinoma context H209; and (4) PTEN TP53-intact sig_a+ high aneuploidy, refining unresolved H243. Interpretation rule remains accept only if signed lower bound >0.15 in registered direction. PTEN claims remain context-dependent; absence of threshold-clearing lineage interaction does not support a lineage-specific PTEN mechanism. All findings are associations among measured variables/analysis-defined strata in the supplied dataset; causal mechanisms, gene-level knockout specificity, and external generalizability remain unsupported. If these new probes are accepted, they strengthen technical and contextual robustness; if not, they constrain PTEN interpretation and reinforce the non-uniform, context-dependent claim."
