  "narrative": "With no due assessments and no remaining validation budget, this explore stage registers a final pre-specified robustness panel rather than additional broad subgroup mining. The panel has two scientifically useful purposes. First, it asks whether the four strongest accepted marginal associations remain threshold-clearing in a simultaneously high-technical-quality subset defined by above-median Cas9 activity and above-median screen ROC quality: SMARCA4-loss stronger dependency, KEAP1-loss weaker dependency, TP53-loss weaker dependency, and MSI-high stronger dependency. These are dataset-internal associations, not causal knockout effects or generalizable biological claims. Second, it probes the least-settled claim, PTEN-loss dependency, in the most supported context after removing the three strongest accepted drivers and signature-negative backgrounds: TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact, SMARCA4-intact, research_signature_a-positive lines. The high-quality screen ROC and high Cas9 complements were already tested; here I request lower-screen-quality and lower-Cas9-quality complements plus high- and lower-screen_nnmd strata. Falsifiable expectation: if PTEN-loss is a context-specific measured predictor rather than a screen-quality artifact, its stronger-dependency contrast should remain detectable in several of these complements, though it may be attenuated and possibly unresolved if cells are smaller. If low-quality strata are negative or unresolved, that would support describing PTEN context effects as quality-sensitive rather than uniform. Alternative interpretation for any accepted result remains residual confounding among correlated genomic, technical, and constructed-signature features. Direction convention: direction -1 claims a more negative exposed-minus-comparator dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency; direction +1 claims less negative/more positive score, i.e. weaker dependency. Returned estimates and intervals are already signed to these hypothesis directions. I will interpret results only if all comparison cells contain at least 20 observations and the signed 95% Welch lower bound exceeds the 0.15 composite-dependency-unit threshold.",
  "research_notes": "ITER20 FINAL ROBUSTNESS PANEL. Validation budget exhausted; no due assessments. Core accepted remains SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency (H5 validated R13; many strata), KEAP1 loss weaker dependency (H7 validated R26; many strata), MSI-high stronger dependency (H41 R75; H90 validated R93), TP53 loss weaker dependency (H3 validated R39), with accepted attenuation of TP53-loss contrast in elevated research_signature_a and research_signature_b contexts (H104 validated R120; H82 validated R79). PTEN loss is context-specific, strongest in TP53-intact research_signature_a-positive backgrounds (H117 validated R131; H58 validated R53; H67 validated R66), with accepted triple-intact high-aneuploidy/low-aneuploidy, screen-quality, Cas9-quality, squamous, and TP53-intact sig_a high-aneuploidy strata; broad global PTEN claims and some lineage/unconditioned contexts remain unresolved or subthreshold. Current panel tests: (1-4) SMARCA4/KEAP1/TP53/MSI in high Cas9 + high screen ROC subset; (5-8) PTEN-loss in triple-intact TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact sig_a-positive lines under lower screen ROC, lower Cas9, higher screen_nnmd, and lower screen_nnmd. Interpret with 0.15 threshold and cell_n >=20; conclusions remain noncausal dataset-internal associations, not mechanism or generalizability."
