gative, high-ploidy lines, +0.624 [0.477, 0.771]. Together these reinforce the context-specific PTEN interpretation: PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency mainly in TP53-intact, research_signature_a-positive backgrounds, especially under additional genomic or technical strata, not as a uniform global predictor. H273/R251 is the exception. The squamous-versus-adenocarcinoma PTEN interaction within TP53-intact, research_signature_a nonnegative lines has signed estimate +0.250 but lower bound -0.037 [interval -0.037 to +0.537] and small exposed squamous cell n=31. The point estimate is nominally in the claimed direction, but the lower bound is far below threshold and the interval includes no interaction and the opposite direction. This is insufficient to accept the interaction and insufficient to reject it as absent because of imprecision; I record it as unresolved/closed. Audit considerations: the predictors appear measured before or independent of the composite outcome, so direct outcome leakage is not evident. However, complete-QC, serum, ploidy, signature, and lineage strata may encode selection or correlated biology; the nominal 95% Welch intervals are not fully adjusted for the extensive exploratory subgroup history. Accepted results should therefore remain described as dataset-internal measured associations among measured predictors and analysis-defined strata, not causal knockout claims, single-gene mechanisms, pathway claims, or generalizable biomarker conclusions. No validation request is made because independent validation capacity is exhausted.",
