point estimate above threshold but an interval crossing zero. Core SMARCA4, KEAP1, and TP53 associations remain accepted within PTEN-loss lines H292/R270, H293/R271, and H294/R272. Remaining unresolved issues include PTEN lineage contexts, MSI-high within TP53-loss, several borderline PTEN clean-background contrasts, and probes lacking valid returned evidence. All conclusions are dataset-internal measured associations among measured predictors and analysis-defined strata. Causality, mechanism, single-gene interpretation, pathway interpretation, and generalizability remain unsupported. Validation capacity is exhausted, so no further validation was requested. Future external priority: adjusted holdout modeling of PTEN-loss effects conditional on TP53-intact and research_signature_a-positive status, adjusted for MSI-high, signature_c, lineage, ploidy, and quality, plus adequately powered MSI-high-by-TP53-loss interaction."
